{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776345023,"nonce":"kAyb5PuSnCZS5QFEvsy0spWvnFA=","title":"Add exponential backoff retry for transient API errors (500, 429)","message":"## Problem\n\nWhen API returns transient errors (500, 502, 503, 504, 429 rate limit), the agent fails without retry. Currently 429 triggers `suspended:auth-failure` but should retry instead.\n\n## Design (Option C)\n\nTwo-tier retry:\n\n1. **Inline retry in agent adapter** (quick recovery):\n   - Detect 500/502/503/504/429 errors in agent output\n   - Wait with exponential backoff: 30s → 60s → 120s\n   - Max 3 retries before escalating\n   - Silent (log only, no telegram notification)\n\n2. **Escalate to session suspend** (persistent failures):\n   - After 3 inline retries fail, emit `AUTH_FAILURE` event\n   - Session transitions to `suspended:api-error`\n   - Watcher retries with longer backoff (existing mechanism)\n\n## Tests (write first, must fail before implementation)\n- tests/test_base_agent.py::test_retries_on_500_error\n  Assert: agent retries 3 times with backoff before emitting AUTH_FAILURE\n- tests/test_base_agent.py::test_retries_on_429_rate_limit\n  Assert: 429 triggers retry, not immediate AUTH_FAILURE\n- tests/test_base_agent.py::test_backoff_delays_increase\n  Assert: delays are 30s, 60s, 120s\n- tests/test_base_agent.py::test_success_after_retry_continues\n  Assert: if retry succeeds, agent continues normally\n\n## Files\n- adapters/agents/base.py (add retry logic to HeadlessAgentBase)\n- tests/test_base_agent.py (new test file or add to existing)\n\n## Implementation\n1. Add `TRANSIENT_ERROR_PATTERNS` tuple to HeadlessAgentBase:\n   - \"500\", \"502\", \"503\", \"504\", \"429\", \"rate limit\", \"overloaded\", \"service unavailable\"\n2. Add `_is_transient_error(text)` classmethod (like `_is_auth_failure`)\n3. In stream loop, when transient error detected:\n   - Log warning\n   - Sleep with backoff (30, 60, 120s)\n   - Restart agent process\n   - Increment retry counter\n4. After 3 retries, emit AUTH_FAILURE to trigger session suspend\n5. Move 429/rate_limit from AUTH_FAILURE_PATTERNS to TRANSIENT_ERROR_PATTERNS\n\n## Backoff parameters (hardcoded)\n```python\nTRANSIENT_RETRY_DELAYS = [30, 60, 120]  # seconds\nMAX_TRANSIENT_RETRIES = 3\n```\n\nREQ: REQ-031","files":null}]}